{"id": "b_work", "query": "Summarise my professional work experience across the companies and ventures I've been part of.", "key_facts": ["Co-founded Seed Savers Club, a peer-to-peer community to help farmers adopt progressive/organic agriculture (~2021-2022)", "Worked at Thrive on consumer commerce / product (discovery, roadmap, growth)", "Worked at Almabase in a product role", "Held a product role at goSTOPS"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_religion", "query": "How has my thinking on religion evolved over the years?", "key_facts": ["Started as an atheist — a personal choice not to believe in god or organised religion", "Grew into anti-theism: a deeper aversion to / hatred of god and organised religion", "Redefines religion as a private, personal set of foundational beliefs and rituals that needs no god", "Critiques organised religion as a tool of social control that externalises agency / enables abuse"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_ideas", "query": "What are the various product or startup ideas I have explored?", "key_facts": ["Seed Savers Club / a community platform for farmers", "The Indian gifting industry (social / D2C gifting)", "web3 communities vs companies", "An AI memory system / hierarchical memory engine"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_ai_memory", "query": "Summarise my views on AI and memory systems.", "key_facts": ["Memory is the next paradigm shift in AI — it becomes the moat via switching cost", "Current memory structures (snippets, chats) are insufficient; memory must be hierarchical or graph-based", "Debugging is the real test of AI coding — where things fail and how fast you find what broke", "A concept-then-residual approach: match high-level concepts, subtract them as background, focus on what is novel"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_capitalism", "query": "What is my critique of capitalism and crony capitalism?", "key_facts": ["I self-identify as a capitalist — reward should be proportional to value created", "But resource seizure (e.g. oil found under someone's razed home) imposes uncompensated costs — the fairness problem", "Crony capitalism drives a growth-welfare decoupling: fast growth but gains concentrated (bottom 50% income share fell)", "India bypassed labour-intensive manufacturing, creating a narrow high-income stratum without absorbing labour"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_labour", "query": "How do I connect employment, gig work, and slavery as forms of coercion?", "key_facts": ["Modern employment is argued to be a form of slavery (bonds, contracts, little freedom)", "Resource monopoly and an artificial crisis force people into employment servitude", "Gig work is economic coercion / coercive labour", "Qualifier: not all employment equals slavery — cooperation toward common goals needs hierarchy"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_pm", "query": "What is my philosophy of product management and what makes an effective PM?", "key_facts": ["Discovered product management as his calling through Marty Cagan's book; great products are the means to the purpose of creating a better world", "What separates better PMs is asking the right questions of data — granular funnel/cohort segmentation, A/B testing, and behavioural insight", "Customer-obsession over metric-chasing: small 5-10% metric gains are insufficient; a customer-focused approach yields drastic improvements", "Problem-validation discipline: validate cohort/problem/solution fit, and conflating different problems and users is hazardous"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_career", "query": "How do I reflect on my own career growth, identity, and the kind of builder I want to be?", "key_facts": ["Career/life follows predictable ~6-7 year cycles of learning that lead to recognizable success", "Feels anxiety and dissatisfaction even after securing what he wanted — a desired role with product, tech, growth, and leadership scope", "Tension between an artist mindset (unconstrained, aesthetic) and a scientist mindset (validate ideas via facts/evidence), with a critique that PM culture rewards salesmanship over truth-seeking", "Conviction enables entrepreneurial bets and fundraising, but honest self-interrogation and objective frameworks are needed beyond self-belief alone"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_relationships", "query": "How do I think about romantic relationships and relationship contracts?", "key_facts": ["Relationships are binding contracts containing both said and unsaid terms and conditions", "Relationships can exist independently of love; compromise relationships become unsatisfying", "Toxicity stems from unilateral contract changes without communication and from two incompatible contract interpretations", "Embedded patriarchal power imbalance is a source of relationship toxicity"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_farming", "query": "Summarise my views on natural/organic farming and the barriers to organic adoption.", "key_facts": ["Bullish on natural farming: farmers should reduce dependency on external inputs and use preventive organic measures that cost less than treating damage", "The primary adoption barrier is skill implementation rather than awareness; organic yields are lower and diversification needs investment without immediate returns", "Fair market price is the critical unsolved problem — geographic dispersal and partial organicity prevent realising a price premium", "Training and mentorship deliver lifetime value and accelerate success; hyperlocal peer communities provide low-cost inputs, labour, knowledge, and better prices"], "hard": true}
{"id": "b_community", "query": "What are my views on how communities should enable knowledge flow and peer-to-peer learning?", "key_facts": ["Communities consist of people at different expertise levels; knowledge must flow both top-to-bottom and peer-to-peer", "Traditional EdTech only solves expert-to-individual connection; it must instead enable peer-to-peer learning and resource exchange within communities", "Regular live sessions and direct engagement between members sustain a community", "Hyperlocal communities are crucial (especially for farmers), providing low-cost inputs, labour, knowledge, and better prices"], "hard": true}
